items/thm-composition-with-a-continuous-function.md-54-
items/thm-composition-with-a-continuous-function.md-55-[L1] Riemann's criterion: a bounded $u$ on $[a,b]$ is integrable if and only if for every real $\eta > 0$ there is a partition $P$ with $U(u,P) - L(u,P) < \eta$ ([[thm-riemann-criterion]], [[def-darboux-integral]]).
items/thm-composition-with-a-continuous-function.md-56-
items/thm-composition-with-a-continuous-function.md:57:[L2] For a partition $P = (n,t)$ of $[a,b]$ and bounded $u$: $U(u,P) - L(u,P) = \sum_{i<n}\bigl(M_i(u) - m_i(u)\bigr)\Delta_i$ with $\Delta_i > 0$ and $\sum_{i<n}\Delta_i = b - a$, and $M_i(u) - m_i(u) = \omega_u(I_i) = \sup\{\,|u(x)-u(y)| : x,y \in I_i\,\}$ ([[def-darboux-sums]], [[def-oscillation]], [[def-partition-and-refinement]], [[def-finite-sum]], [[lem-finite-sum-laws]]).
items/thm-composition-with-a-continuous-function.md-58-
items/thm-composition-with-a-continuous-function.md-59-[L3] $[m,M]$ with $m \le M$ and $[a,b]$ are closed bounded intervals, hence compact ([[thm-heine-borel-r]], [[def-open-cover-r]], [[def-interval]]).
items/thm-composition-with-a-continuous-function.md-60-
